@startuml
title install-process-builder - install and verify the outcome
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Developer / agent" as Dev
participant "InstallProcessBuilderCommand" as Cmd
participant "Bundled archive (.gz)" as FS
participant "IPackageInstaller" as Inst
participant "Creatio" as Crt
participant "IServerReadinessWaiter" as Wait
participant "ProcessDesignServiceOutcomeVerifier" as Ver

Dev -> Cmd : install-process-builder -e env
Cmd -> FS : is the archive present?
alt archive missing
  FS --> Cmd : no
  Cmd --> Dev : "this clio distribution carries no archive,\nretrying will not help" (exit 1)
end
Cmd -> Inst : Install(gz, createBackup = true)
note right of Cmd
  DeveloperModeEnabled = false:
  otherwise the unlock step routes
  through cliogate and fails
end note
Inst -> Crt : upload + install package
Crt -> Crt : configuration build\n(the package ships SOURCE ONLY)
Crt --> Inst : archive accepted
note over Crt
  the platform restarts itself:
  .NET Framework - workspace assembly changed
  .NET - the installer issues the restart
end note
Cmd -> Wait : WaitForReady (health check, 600 s budget)
Wait --> Cmd : the instance is back
Cmd -> Ver : IsPackageOperational("CrtProcessBuilder")
Ver -> Crt : POST /rest/ProcessDesignService/Ping
note right of Ver
  3 attempts, 5 s apart, 15 s timeout.
  The operation is UNGATED - it proves
  the build, not the caller's permissions
end note
Crt --> Ver : version of the assembly actually serving
Ver --> Cmd : operational / diagnosis
Cmd --> Dev : "Done" (exit 0) or diagnosis (exit 1)
@enduml
